# Frozen 2026-09-15, the first run with --ratchets on. Comment blocks over the
# 10-line limit that predate the gate; the rule from here is two lines at the
# point of use, with anything longer moving into a doc and leaving a pointer.
# Two-way: shrink a block or delete it and its line here goes STALE, which
# fails - so remove the line in the same change.
#
# Format: <file>	<first comment line, 60 chars>.
# third_party/ANTfrastructure/docs/code-quality-tooling.md#comment-size-comment-size
#
# WHAT THESE ARE. Nine of the ten are script HEADERS, and in this repo a header
# is the only place a decision is written down: why the lint wrapper passes the
# consumer root explicitly, why the renovate wrapper is a local CLI, why every
# build write in the container goes to a container-local path. The audit that
# produced them asked for exactly that. They are frozen rather than shortened
# because moving one needs a docs/ page to move it INTO, and this repo has no
# docs/ tree yet - that is its own change, not a line in a ratchet commit.
#
# THE TWO MID-FILE BLOCKS are different and both are real candidates to shrink:
# ci-container-steps.sh:70 (the CARGO_CLIPPY_ARGS rationale) and
# run-producer-pi.sh:169 (the hub loader paths) each explain one decision that
# now has an upstream home.

